xmodel/grok-td7-law-review.md:21:  - Those pins force \(\Pi_e\) to run over *nonzero* arrivals only (a 0-edge inside \(\Pi_e\) would contribute \(\eta^{\nu\mu_0}\) and give \(d_p=\mu_0+\nu\mu_0+\nu\), contradicting \(d_p=\mu+\nu\)). Combined with \(k=0\), \(r_0=1\), \(\mu_1=1\), this is exactly (1), with \(\ell:=(d_q-1)/\nu-1\) the R2.2 extra-orbit count. R1.0 already gives \(d_q\equiv1\pmod\nu\), so \(\ell\in\mathbb{Z}\). \(d_q/d_p=\bar\kappa/(\bar\kappa-2)>1\) forces \(\ell\geq1\) on the whole book (an \(\ell=0\) cell would have \(d_q=1+\nu\le d_p\)).
