xmodel/grok-nfz-final.md:21:  **The free tail does not start from `α_entry`.** §3 threads the register in global gap order — the merge of the word’s `γ` sequence with the skeleton. `θ*` is the *minimum* skeleton competing gap, so the last pre-tail death is the skeleton vertex that attains `θ*`. Z1 gives `α_* = ℓ+1−θ*` after that death. For the td-7 direct skeleton, `θ* = 1/13566` and `17, 19 | 13566`. The numerator of `ℓ+1−1/13566` is `≡ −1 (mod 17)` and `(mod 19)`, so those primes **never cancel**: `17·19 | den(α_*)` after G, for every incoming register. Independently replayed on the real interleaving of `Z = (3,5,7,9,11)` at `P_0 = 2` with `{2/5, 1/34, 3/3230, 2/11305, 1/13566}`:
