+
+The D23 posterior is not based merely on an equation count.  The exact NF
+calculation in Section 3 shows that the apparent six compatibility equations
+have only five effective conditions: two solve auxiliary differences and
+three constrain the D21 base.  If the resulting ideal is proper, its D21-base
+dimension is at least `13-3=10`, and the row22red variety has at least five
+additional free directions, hence dimension at least 15.  The 0/12 base-point
+filter is exactly what one expects from a positive-codimension sublocus over a
+field of size about `10^5`; it is weak evidence for a unit ideal.
+
+## 2. D23: the exact objects and the wrong-object boundary
+
+There are four distinct objects in play.
+
+1. `directionb_core23_p105337.ms` is the 87-variable unspecialized modular
+   D23 hybrid.  It retains `A1,A2,HW1,HW2` and their radical/guard data.  This
+   is the modular object closest to the full finite-radical chart.  Its long
+   extension was shed without a verdict.
+2. `directionb_row22compat_p*.ms` is 72 variables and 54 equations, but
+   `cases/directionb_row22_emit.py` calls `FC.radical_point(p)` and substitutes
+   one cube root for each `Ai` and one sign for each `HWi/Wi`.  It is one of
+   the `3*3*2*2=36` radical fibers.
+3. `directionb_row22red_p*.ms` is the exact 29-variable pivot-eliminated form
+   of that same fixed radical fiber.  Its variety is the 72v compatibility
+   variety times the recorded affine pivot factor in the direction appropriate
+   to the reconstruction; it is not equivalent to the unspecialized 87v
+   object.
+4. `directionb_fiber_gb_p105337.out.txt` is the reduced grevlex GB of D21 on
+   that representative radical fiber.  The tracked local artifact exists only
+   for `p=105337`.
+
+The phrase “fiber GB” is easy to misread.  It is **not** a GB at one fixed D21
+base point.  It describes the whole 13-dimensional D21 locus after the finite
+radical coordinates have been specialized.  Conversely, it is not a
+parametric GB whose 13 directions are coefficient parameters: those directions
+are ordinary quotient-ring variables.  It is also not a 397-dimensional
+vector-space basis and not a list of 397 points.
+
+The exact banked ring is
+
+```text
+R0 = F_105337[
+ x68,x70,x71,x72,x73,x47,x52,x53,x54,x55,x57,x58,x59,x60,
+ x62,x63,x65,x66,W1,W2,uW1,uW2
+]
+```
+
+in precisely that grevlex variable order.  The 397 polynomials contain
+282,304 terms.  `A1,A2` and the ratios `HWi/Wi` have been specialized, while
+`W1,W2` remain symbolic and invertible through `uWi*Wi-1`.  The basis pins
+quartics for `W1,W2`; therefore it covers all 16 pole-scale root branches over
+the algebraic closure inside this radical fiber, not just one `W` point.
+
+Consequently, a current `[1]` would be important but fiber-local.  It would not
+kill the other 35 radical fibers, the conjugate `sqrt(3)` embedding absent a
+proved transport, characteristic zero, B-unfrozen residue A, or JC2.  Equal
+support and equal census on the 36 D21 fibers do not prove ideal isomorphism.
+For EMPTY, either enumerate the full cover or prove an explicit symmetry that
+transports the equations and saturation guards.
+
+## 3. The NF quick shot: exact result and best software move
+
+### 3.1 Which rows can be reduced
+
+The six raw rows of the 72v compatibility object do not live in `R0`: they
+still contain the 22 pivot coordinates.  Reducing them directly against the
+397-element basis is a wrong-ring operation.
+
+The correct targets are equations 24--29 (zero-based) of
+`directionb_row22red_p105337.ms`.  They live in
+
+```text
+S = R0[x16,x17,x24,x25,x32,x37,x69].
+```
+
+The banked GB embeds canonically in `S` and remains a GB because the extended
+grevlex order restricts to the banked order on `R0`.  The seven new variables
+must remain polynomial variables; treating them as a coefficient field would
+silently invert nonunits and change emptiness.
+
+### 3.2 What a constant NF would prove
+
+Let `I21=<G>` and let `c_i` be one correct post-pivot compatibility row.  If
+
+```text
+NF_G(c_i) = lambda,       lambda in F_105337^*,
+```
+
+then `c_i-lambda` lies in `I21*S`, so
+
+```text
+I21*S + <c_i> = S.
+```
+
+Thus even one nonzero constant NF would prove that the compatibility
+intersection is empty on the **entire representative fixed-radical D21
+locus**, uniformly in all seven auxiliary variables and all symbolic `W`
+branches.  A zero NF would say that row is redundant.  A nonconstant NF says
+nothing alone: several nonconstant remainders may jointly generate 1, or may
+have a large common zero set.
+
+Even a constant would not prove the full D23 kill for the scope reasons in
+Section 2.  Repeating it at three primes would still be modular evidence, not
+an exact characteristic-zero identity.
+
+### 3.3 Actual `p=105337` result
+
+The quick shot is no longer hypothetical.  Exact Singular reduction and
+msolve's known-basis NF mode agree, with all 397 listed leading monomials
+checked against the declared grevlex order.
+
+- None of the six NFs is zero or a nonzero constant.
+- Each row falls from 1,216/1,218 terms and degree 9 to exactly 150 terms and
+  degree 5.
+- All dependence on `x16,x24,x69` disappears.  The other four auxiliary
+  variables occur only through
+
+  ```text
+  d1 = x17-x32,       d2 = x25-x37.
+  ```
+
+- The `6 x 2` coefficient matrix of `(d1,d2)` has rank two everywhere on the
+  chart.  Rows 0 and 1 have minor
+
+  ```text
+  76716*uW1^2*uW2^2,
+  ```
+
+  a unit modulo `uWi*Wi-1`.  There is no determinantal rank-drop boundary on
+  this prime/fiber.
+- Eliminating `d1,d2` initially gives four 10-term, degree-4 core rows
+  `R2,...,R5`, but they satisfy the exact constant syzygy
+
+  ```text
+  77149*R2 + 16527*R3 + 81917*R4 + R5 = 0  (mod 105337).
+  ```
+
+  Their constant row rank is three.
+- Each obstruction is a linear form in only six features:
+
+  ```text
+  (x57-x65)^2*uW1^2,  (x57-x65)^2*uW2^2,
+  x53*uW1,             x58*uW2,             x70, x72.
+  ```
+
+  Notably, `x53,x58,x70,x72` all occur in the banked 13-variable free set.
+  This is not a proof of properness, but it strengthens the NONEMPTY prior.
+
+Therefore, on this prime and radical fiber,
+
+```text
+V(row22red) is empty
+  iff V(I21 + <R2,R3,R4>) is empty.
+```
+
+The five auxiliary directions invisible to the NFs are free; `d1,d2` are
+then recovered uniquely from the first two NFs.  Pivots and the four solved
+deep directions are recovered afterward, with the six deep-kernel directions
+remaining free as prescribed by the rank-four Schur step.
+
+### 3.4 Acceleration ratings
+
+| emission/workflow | rating | reason |
+|---|---:|---|
+| Ordinary solver input: 397 GB polynomials + six unreduced rows | **3/10** | About 290k input terms; an ordinary ideal solve may recompute the GB and all critical-pair structure.  Merely listing a GB is not a warm start. |
+| Known-basis normal forms (`-n 6 -i`, after a toy/version gate) | **10/10** | This is the correct quick shot and completed locally in 0.76 s; Singular independently agrees. |
+| True incremental solve from `G` plus three 10-term rows | **8/10** | Algebraically right, but engine support matters; a classical Singular first increment did not finish inside a three-minute pilot. |
+| **Original 22v D21 fiber core + three 10-term rows** | **10/10, preferred** | Only 29 equations and **5,378 total terms**.  It lets the engine recover the known 397-element D21 basis from the 5,348-term core, previously an 11 s task, without ingesting the 10 MB basis. |
+
+The headline “GB warm start” should therefore be refined:
+
+> Use the banked GB to discover and certify the quotient rows; solve the
+> sparse original D21 generators plus the three quotient obstructions.
+
+Before this becomes a promoted emission, retain division/provenance data for
+`c_i-NF(c_i)`, verify the GB against the original D21 ideal, independently
+reconstruct all six compatibility rows, repeat at the other two primes, and
+repeat on every radical fiber or prove symmetry.  The current GB has no
+cofactor transformation back to the 24 D21 input rows, so the present result
+is an exact modular discovery and solver target, not yet a global proof
+certificate.
+
+## 4. Book-tier and foundation audit
+
+### td-7
+
+The strongest honest reading is: every configuration in the filed 17-cell,
+233-deduplicated-route E5 book is tower-dead, including the stated insertion
+and padding perimeter.  This is a serious theorem relative to the promoted
+Sigray/tower trust set.  The remaining distinction is not “the computation
+might have missed one of its own rows”; it is whether every genuine td-7
+configuration lands in that filed route language.  I would keep “book
+closed” and delete “panel closed” from campaign-level prose until that landing
+statement is made theorem-level.
+
+### td-12
+
+The 14 type-`(3,5)` cell stamps look good at their exact tier: six H8
+spine-deaths and eight first-death refusals.  The perimeter is much weaker
+than td-7.  The document itself exhibits the dangerous `u=1` first death with
+gap `1/3`, which is not refused, and names six other fail-closed classes.
+This is not a closed td-12 book in the ordinary exhaustive sense, and it says
+nothing about the other td-12 entry types.  It is also negative evidence for
+the proposed sharpened slogan “below TD-BOUND means realizable”: the one
+below-bound filed entry dies cheaply.
+
+### td-11
+
+The current controlling record is `TOWER-TD11.md` Sections 17--18, not its
+historical OPEN lists.  FC2/4/5/6/7 are discharged, as are the nested 129 and
+the two-word deep family at their stated tiers.  FC1-R is an expensive
+cap-free compiler problem; FC3 is a mathematical/data-model refile problem
+and remains the real wall.  More compute alone is much more likely to help
+FC1 than FC3.
+
+### G1 and G2
+
+G1 should stop being described as an open mathematical bridge.  A proof by
+contradiction may select the globally minimal GGV counterexample promised by
+the theorem.  What must be removed is the claim that every initially chosen
+counterexample is normalized to that pair, or that its `td` is preserved by
+the global selection.
+
+For G2, `TRANSPORT.md` is real progress: the selected pre-Laurent polynomial
+pair can plausibly carry the rectangular GGV data and a Sigray normal form
+simultaneously.  The remaining G2 is data transport, not coordinate
+transport.  No theorem turns a GGV admissible corner chain into the
+fiber-tagged pole/Eggers--Wall tree consumed by the sheet books.  Polygon
+data may not determine the needed residual cancellation and fiber labels, so
+the desired object may have to be a coefficient-enriched correspondence, not
+a functor from the current ledger alone.
+
+## 5. FC5 versus the Sigray mass bound
+
+### 5.1 The exact interface
+
+Let `s=alpha+beta`.  At a Sigray pole the repository's entry formulas give
+
+```text
+M=b,       kbar=a*s,       rho=a/b,
+w=(kbar-rho)/nu.
+```
+
+Therefore the pole mass has the exact state expression
+
+```text
+             w*M^2
+ab/nu = -----------------.                         (5.1)
+          s*M - 1
+```
+
+Call the right side `Phi_s(w,M)`.  This is the best possible scalar bridge
+from the FC5 state to TD-BOUND.  It is substantially better than comparing
+`w` informally with `ab/nu`.
+
+### 5.2 Why it does not telescope
+
+`Phi_s` is not monotone across the admitted merge arithmetic.
+
+- Residue A has `s=5`, two incoming `(a,b,nu)=(1,1,2)` poles, hence
+  `w=2` and total incoming mass 1.  Its IIa merge has
+  `(r,l,nu_merge)=(2,1,3)`, so `M'=2`, `w'=3/2`, and
+
+  ```text
+  Phi_5(3/2,2)=2/3;       incoming - outgoing = +1/3.
+  ```
+
+- As an arithmetic/printed-tier negative control, the admissible type-`(3,4)`
+  three-pole packet with three `(1,1,3)` poles has `s=7`, `w=2` and total
+  incoming mass 1.  The IIa data `(r,l,nu_merge)=(3,1,2)` give
+  `M'=3`, `w'=8/3`, and
+
+  ```text
+  Phi_7(8/3,3)=6/5;       incoming - outgoing = -1/5.
+  ```
+
+The second packet is not claimed realized by a Keller map; it is enough to
+refute a proof from FC5/MP6 arithmetic alone.  Any valid telescope needs an
+extra signed merge defect, branch history, or proximity contribution.  FC5
+forgets precisely that history when it emits only `(w',M')`.
+
+My rating is therefore:
+
+- direct scalar FC5 proof of `sum ab/nu<=1`: **3–5%**;
+- FC5 as bookkeeping inside a new proximity/intersection invariant:
+  **20–25%** chance of a useful lemma;
+- full G5 closure from this route alone: **<=2%**.
+
+### 5.3 The larger G5 correction
+
+Even a proof of
+
+```text
+sum_F a_F*b_F/nu_F <= 1
+```
+
+would imply only
+
+```text
+td <= alpha*beta
+```
+
+for the selected type.  The cited GGV chain enumeration is finite only after
+an input degree bound; it is not an absolute finite catalog of possible
+`(alpha,beta)`.  Thus `alpha*beta` can still run without a proved bound.  A
+second theorem bounding the selected pair's type/degree is required to close
+foundation G5.  `TDBOUND.md` currently overstates the finite-ladder payoff.
+
+What remains genuinely valuable is the exact resolved-pencil identity
+
+```text
+td/(alpha*beta)
+  = sum_F a_F*b_F/nu_F
+  = (1/2) * sum_p (r_p/alpha-s_p/beta)^2,
+
+Delta^2 = -2*td/(alpha*beta).
+```
+
+The target `Delta^2>=-2` is a Keller/proximity theorem at divergence centers,
+not a consequence of the exceptional lattice alone.  In particular, support
+on an ADE tree is insufficient: already on `A1`, `(2E)^2=-8`.  Any ADE route
+must prove that `Delta` is an actual root (and integral), not merely supported
+on a root lattice.
+
+### 5.4 New G5 experiments
+
+**CONJECTURE P (proximity-source law).**  On a common resolution, put
+`u_p=r_p/alpha-s_p/beta` and change from total multiplicities to proximity
+increments `q=P^{-1}u`.  The constant-Jacobian condition forces `q` to be a
+sum of at most two primitive source packets, one for each infinity direction,
+with squared norm at most 2.  Then `Delta^2>=-2` follows.  FC5 should be tested
+as the local slope/flux update for these packets, not as the potential itself.
+
+This is conjectural.  Its first falsification test is to compute `q` for
+residue A and for the sign-reversing three-pole packet above.  It is sharper
+than “the remaining graph is ADE” because it names the missing source/root
+assertion.
+
+A cheap theorem-discovery gate is to enumerate the symbolic MP6 merge schemas
+and solve for a low-degree augmented potential
+
+```text
+Phi_s(w,M) + schema_charge(history)
+```
+
+whose total is monotone.  The `+1/3` and `-1/5` examples are mandatory
+controls.  If no low-degree invariant survives them and the mixed/ZCH/dirty
+schemas, retire FC5 as a G5 lane rather than enlarging more books.
+
+## 6. Characteristic zero and the formal-germ disproof branch
+
+### 6.1 Characteristic zero
+
+The endpoint in `sol-char0-plan.md` is correct: work over `Q(sqrt(3))`, or
+flatten to `Q[s,...]/(s^2-3)`, and finish with a checked identity
+
+```text
+A = sum_i H_i*F_i + H_s*(s^2-3),       A in Z\{0}.
+```
+
+Do not split `a+s*b=0` into `a=b=0`.  The six-compatibility/quotient route is
+the right certificate target if global modular emptiness lands.
+
+The trigger needs correction.  A `[1]` from the current 72v/29v lane is one
+finite radical fiber.  It cannot trigger a global char-0 certificate unless
+the remaining fibers are exhausted and recombined (with idempotents/Galois
+descent), or the unspecialized radical variables are restored.  The 397 GB is
+also unsuitable as proof provenance: it is positive-dimensional,
+finite-field, fixed-radical, and has no transformation to the original rows.
+Use it to discover NFs, never as if its coefficients lifted canonically to a
+global characteristic-zero certificate.
+
+If the sparse three-obstruction system is `[1]` on one fiber, first obtain a
+modular cofactor DAG back to the six rows and the D21 generators.  Then decide
+whether an exact fiber certificate or an unspecialized radical-algebra
+certificate is cheaper.  If it is NONEMPTY, verify a point through `d1,d2`,
+pivots, four solved deep variables, the six-dimensional deep kernel, all 72
+rows, the 87-row hybrid and every saturation guard before discussing a lift.
+
+### 6.2 Formal germs
+
+The kill direction is unconditional at the stated window scope: a formal
+germ has every finite truncation, so an empty `V_D` rules it out.
+
+The live direction in `DEPTH-STAB.md` is not currently safe for promotion.
+
+1. Stabilization of elimination **closures** does not by itself stabilize
+   constructible images or produce a compatible inverse-limit point.
+2. The stated König argument concerns finite `F_p` point sets, whereas an
+   msolve NONEMPTY verdict is over `Fbar_p`; that tree is not finitely
+   branching in the asserted sense.
+3. The emitted scalar `.ms` Jacobian has no uniformizer.  Unit derivatives of
+   pivot, radical or Rabinowitsch rows can create a spurious `e=0`.  The
+   original series-valued map, a square function block, and a theorem placing
+   surplus equations in its completed ideal are still missing.
+
+The correct positive certificate is a smooth point of the original
+series-valued system together with a valid Hensel/Tougeron or finite-type
+Greenberg bridge.  Even then the output is a mod-p formal germ on a named
+B-frozen chart.  The remaining chain is
+
+```text
+mod-p formal germ
+ -> compatible characteristic-zero germ
+ -> all places / B-unfrozen / all depths
+ -> convergent or algebraic branches
+ -> global polynomial Keller pair
+ -> verified nonautomorphism.
+```
+
+No current Hermite--Padé result supplies these arrows: the banked full-rank
+tests kill chosen completions, while the general D23 prefix has enough future
+coefficients to admit bounded algebraic extensions separately on each side.
+
+## 7. New independent avenues and recommended order
+
+### 7.1 Radical-fiber NF atlas — immediate
+
+Build the sparse three-obstruction object at the other two primes and across
+all 36 radical fibers.  D21 representative fibers previously solved in about
+11 s and had identical censuses, so this is a much cheaper way to test the
+finite cover than six more 12-hour raw runs.  Hash the three-row feature
+matrices.  If they are related by explicit substitutions, promote that
+substitution as the missing symmetry proof; do not infer symmetry from equal
+counts.
+
+For a NONEMPTY branch, do not sample arbitrary D21 points: the target is
+codimension at most three in the 13-fold, so random points almost never hit
+it.  Instead impose the three obstruction rows first and take generic slices
+in the remaining Noether-normalization directions.  One verified point on
+one fiber is enough to refute a full D23 kill.
+
+### 7.2 Exact Euler-characteristic identity — new global lane
+
+Let `S=A(F)` be the nonproperness curve and `U=A^2\S`.  For a Keller map, the
+restriction
+
+```text
+F^{-1}(U) -> U
+```
+
+is a finite etale cover of degree `td`.  Additivity and multiplicativity of
+compactly supported Euler characteristic give the exact identity
+
+```text
+1 - chi_c(F^{-1}(S)) = td * (1 - chi_c(S)).          (7.1)
+```
+
+**CONJECTURAL USE E.**  Jelonek's rational one-place components, together
+with the Sigray dicritical maps and their intersections, make both Euler
+characteristics in (7.1) computable or sharply bounded from the pole tree;
+the resulting divisibility/sign constraints bound `td` or kill residue A.
+
+The identity is exact; the claimed computability and leverage are
+conjectural.  I rate a useful obstruction at **10–15%**.  Its advantage is
+that it sees the whole nonproperness curve rather than one fixed generic
+fiber passport.  The first pilot should use the already enumerated residue-A
+B/x component menus and must include component intersections and exceptional
+preimages, not just count components.
+
+### 7.3 Overall order
+
+1. Emit and certify `D21 core + R2,R3,R4` at `p=105337`; race a proper-basis
+   solve and a conditioned witness extraction.
+2. Repeat the NF/three-row derivation at the other primes and the 36 radical
+   fibers; search for an actual symmetry while doing so.
+3. If any fiber is NONEMPTY, reconstruct a full D23 point before D25 or any
+   valuation-`e` work.  Repair the series-valued lift theorem in parallel.
+4. If every fiber is EMPTY, switch immediately to the exact
+   `Q(sqrt(3))`/radical-algebra certificate plan with full provenance.
+5. On the global proof side, fund the proximity-source and Euler-characteristic
+   pilots.  Do not count TD-BOUND as G5 until an independent absolute type
+   bound exists.
+
+My independent bottom line is that the current data lean toward a large
+fixed-fiber D23 survivor, not a kill.  That would be valuable: the new
+three-obstruction description is far sharper than a 29-variable proper GB.
+But it would still be a local modular window survivor.  The campaign should
+make the next claim exactly as large as the object just computed, and no
+larger.

