+The D23 posterior is not based merely on an equation count.  The exact NF
+calculation in Section 3 shows that the apparent six compatibility equations
+have only five effective conditions: two solve auxiliary differences and
+three constrain the D21 base.  If the resulting ideal is proper, its D21-base
+dimension is at least `13-3=10`, and the row22red variety has at least five
+additional free directions, hence dimension at least 15.  The 0/12 base-point
+filter is exactly what one expects from a positive-codimension sublocus over a
+field of size about `10^5`; it is weak evidence for a unit ideal.
