+
+## 5. FC5 versus the Sigray mass bound
+
+### 5.1 The exact interface
+
+Let `s=alpha+beta`.  At a Sigray pole the repository's entry formulas give
+
+```text
+M=b,       kbar=a*s,       rho=a/b,
+w=(kbar-rho)/nu.
+```
+
+Therefore the pole mass has the exact state expression
+
+```text
+             w*M^2
+ab/nu = -----------------.                         (5.1)
+          s*M - 1
+```
+
+Call the right side `Phi_s(w,M)`.  This is the best possible scalar bridge
+from the FC5 state to TD-BOUND.  It is substantially better than comparing
+`w` informally with `ab/nu`.
+
+### 5.2 Why it does not telescope
+
+`Phi_s` is not monotone across the admitted merge arithmetic.
+
+- Residue A has `s=5`, two incoming `(a,b,nu)=(1,1,2)` poles, hence
+  `w=2` and total incoming mass 1.  Its IIa merge has
+  `(r,l,nu_merge)=(2,1,3)`, so `M'=2`, `w'=3/2`, and
+
+  ```text
+  Phi_5(3/2,2)=2/3;       incoming - outgoing = +1/3.
+  ```
+
+- As an arithmetic/printed-tier negative control, the admissible type-`(3,4)`
+  three-pole packet with three `(1,1,3)` poles has `s=7`, `w=2` and total
+  incoming mass 1.  The IIa data `(r,l,nu_merge)=(3,1,2)` give
+  `M'=3`, `w'=8/3`, and
+
+  ```text
+  Phi_7(8/3,3)=6/5;       incoming - outgoing = -1/5.
+  ```
+
+The second packet is not claimed realized by a Keller map; it is enough to
+refute a proof from FC5/MP6 arithmetic alone.  Any valid telescope needs an
+extra signed merge defect, branch history, or proximity contribution.  FC5
+forgets precisely that history when it emits only `(w',M')`.
+
+My rating is therefore:
+
+- direct scalar FC5 proof of `sum ab/nu<=1`: **3–5%**;
+- FC5 as bookkeeping inside a new proximity/intersection invariant:
+  **20–25%** chance of a useful lemma;
+- full G5 closure from this route alone: **<=2%**.
+
+### 5.3 The larger G5 correction
+
+Even a proof of
+
+```text
+sum_F a_F*b_F/nu_F <= 1
+```
+
+would imply only
+
+```text
+td <= alpha*beta
+```
+
+for the selected type.  The cited GGV chain enumeration is finite only after
+an input degree bound; it is not an absolute finite catalog of possible
+`(alpha,beta)`.  Thus `alpha*beta` can still run without a proved bound.  A
+second theorem bounding the selected pair's type/degree is required to close
+foundation G5.  `TDBOUND.md` currently overstates the finite-ladder payoff.
+
+What remains genuinely valuable is the exact resolved-pencil identity
+
+```text
+td/(alpha*beta)
+  = sum_F a_F*b_F/nu_F
+  = (1/2) * sum_p (r_p/alpha-s_p/beta)^2,
+
+Delta^2 = -2*td/(alpha*beta).
+```
+
+The target `Delta^2>=-2` is a Keller/proximity theorem at divergence centers,
+not a consequence of the exceptional lattice alone.  In particular, support
+on an ADE tree is insufficient: already on `A1`, `(2E)^2=-8`.  Any ADE route
+must prove that `Delta` is an actual root (and integral), not merely supported
+on a root lattice.
+
+### 5.4 New G5 experiments
+
+**CONJECTURE P (proximity-source law).**  On a common resolution, put
+`u_p=r_p/alpha-s_p/beta` and change from total multiplicities to proximity
+increments `q=P^{-1}u`.  The constant-Jacobian condition forces `q` to be a
+sum of at most two primitive source packets, one for each infinity direction,
+with squared norm at most 2.  Then `Delta^2>=-2` follows.  FC5 should be tested
+as the local slope/flux update for these packets, not as the potential itself.
+
+This is conjectural.  Its first falsification test is to compute `q` for
+residue A and for the sign-reversing three-pole packet above.  It is sharper
+than “the remaining graph is ADE” because it names the missing source/root
+assertion.
+
+A cheap theorem-discovery gate is to enumerate the symbolic MP6 merge schemas
+and solve for a low-degree augmented potential
+
+```text
+Phi_s(w,M) + schema_charge(history)
+```
+
+whose total is monotone.  The `+1/3` and `-1/5` examples are mandatory
+controls.  If no low-degree invariant survives them and the mixed/ZCH/dirty
+schemas, retire FC5 as a G5 lane rather than enlarging more books.
+
+## 6. Characteristic zero and the formal-germ disproof branch
+
+### 6.1 Characteristic zero
+
+The endpoint in `sol-char0-plan.md` is correct: work over `Q(sqrt(3))`, or
+flatten to `Q[s,...]/(s^2-3)`, and finish with a checked identity
+
+```text
+A = sum_i H_i*F_i + H_s*(s^2-3),       A in Z\{0}.
+```
+
+Do not split `a+s*b=0` into `a=b=0`.  The six-compatibility/quotient route is
+the right certificate target if global modular emptiness lands.
+
+The trigger needs correction.  A `[1]` from the current 72v/29v lane is one
+finite radical fiber.  It cannot trigger a global char-0 certificate unless
+the remaining fibers are exhausted and recombined (with idempotents/Galois
+descent), or the unspecialized radical variables are restored.  The 397 GB is
+also unsuitable as proof provenance: it is positive-dimensional,
+finite-field, fixed-radical, and has no transformation to the original rows.
+Use it to discover NFs, never as if its coefficients lifted canonically to a
+global characteristic-zero certificate.
+
+If the sparse three-obstruction system is `[1]` on one fiber, first obtain a
+modular cofactor DAG back to the six rows and the D21 generators.  Then decide
+whether an exact fiber certificate or an unspecialized radical-algebra
+certificate is cheaper.  If it is NONEMPTY, verify a point through `d1,d2`,
+pivots, four solved deep variables, the six-dimensional deep kernel, all 72
+rows, the 87-row hybrid and every saturation guard before discussing a lift.
+
+### 6.2 Formal germs
+
+The kill direction is unconditional at the stated window scope: a formal
+germ has every finite truncation, so an empty `V_D` rules it out.
+
+The live direction in `DEPTH-STAB.md` is not currently safe for promotion.
+
+1. Stabilization of elimination **closures** does not by itself stabilize
+   constructible images or produce a compatible inverse-limit point.
+2. The stated König argument concerns finite `F_p` point sets, whereas an
+   msolve NONEMPTY verdict is over `Fbar_p`; that tree is not finitely
+   branching in the asserted sense.
+3. The emitted scalar `.ms` Jacobian has no uniformizer.  Unit derivatives of
+   pivot, radical or Rabinowitsch rows can create a spurious `e=0`.  The
+   original series-valued map, a square function block, and a theorem placing
+   surplus equations in its completed ideal are still missing.
+
+The correct positive certificate is a smooth point of the original
+series-valued system together with a valid Hensel/Tougeron or finite-type
+Greenberg bridge.  Even then the output is a mod-p formal germ on a named
+B-frozen chart.  The remaining chain is
+
+```text
+mod-p formal germ
+ -> compatible characteristic-zero germ
+ -> all places / B-unfrozen / all depths
+ -> convergent or algebraic branches
+ -> global polynomial Keller pair
+ -> verified nonautomorphism.
+```
+
+No current Hermite--Padé result supplies these arrows: the banked full-rank
+tests kill chosen completions, while the general D23 prefix has enough future
+coefficients to admit bounded algebraic extensions separately on each side.
+
+## 7. New independent avenues and recommended order
+
+### 7.1 Radical-fiber NF atlas — immediate
+
+Build the sparse three-obstruction object at the other two primes and across
+all 36 radical fibers.  D21 representative fibers previously solved in about
+11 s and had identical censuses, so this is a much cheaper way to test the
+finite cover than six more 12-hour raw runs.  Hash the three-row feature
+matrices.  If they are related by explicit substitutions, promote that
+substitution as the missing symmetry proof; do not infer symmetry from equal
+counts.
+
+For a NONEMPTY branch, do not sample arbitrary D21 points: the target is
+codimension at most three in the 13-fold, so random points almost never hit
+it.  Instead impose the three obstruction rows first and take generic slices
+in the remaining Noether-normalization directions.  One verified point on
+one fiber is enough to refute a full D23 kill.
+
+### 7.2 Exact Euler-characteristic identity — new global lane
+
+Let `S=A(F)` be the nonproperness curve and `U=A^2\S`.  For a Keller map, the
+restriction
+
+```text
+F^{-1}(U) -> U
+```
+
+is a finite etale cover of degree `td`.  Additivity and multiplicativity of
+compactly supported Euler characteristic give the exact identity
+
+```text
+1 - chi_c(F^{-1}(S)) = td * (1 - chi_c(S)).          (7.1)
+```
+
+**CONJECTURAL USE E.**  Jelonek's rational one-place components, together
+with the Sigray dicritical maps and their intersections, make both Euler
+characteristics in (7.1) computable or sharply bounded from the pole tree;
+the resulting divisibility/sign constraints bound `td` or kill residue A.
+
+The identity is exact; the claimed computability and leverage are
+conjectural.  I rate a useful obstruction at **10–15%**.  Its advantage is
+that it sees the whole nonproperness curve rather than one fixed generic
+fiber passport.  The first pilot should use the already enumerated residue-A
+B/x component menus and must include component intersections and exceptional
+preimages, not just count components.
+
+### 7.3 Overall order
+
+1. Emit and certify `D21 core + R2,R3,R4` at `p=105337`; race a proper-basis
+   solve and a conditioned witness extraction.
+2. Repeat the NF/three-row derivation at the other primes and the 36 radical
+   fibers; search for an actual symmetry while doing so.
+3. If any fiber is NONEMPTY, reconstruct a full D23 point before D25 or any
+   valuation-`e` work.  Repair the series-valued lift theorem in parallel.
+4. If every fiber is EMPTY, switch immediately to the exact
+   `Q(sqrt(3))`/radical-algebra certificate plan with full provenance.
+5. On the global proof side, fund the proximity-source and Euler-characteristic
+   pilots.  Do not count TD-BOUND as G5 until an independent absolute type
+   bound exists.
+
+My independent bottom line is that the current data lean toward a large
+fixed-fiber D23 survivor, not a kill.  That would be valuable: the new
+three-obstruction description is far sharper than a 29-variable proper GB.
+But it would still be a local modular window survivor.  The campaign should
+make the next claim exactly as large as the object just computed, and no
+larger.

